SWEET FG F2 (patch 0157, docs/research/47 stage F2): boot-arg sweetfg=2 = F1, then the first reads of the MAX77759 fuel gauge (I2C 0x36 on HSI2C12): DevName, Status, RepSOC, VCell, Current, AvgCurrent, Temp, RepCap, FullCapRep, TTE, TTF, each as one auto-mode pointer write (no stop) and one 2-byte read (stop), polled, on ABL's clock and timing setup (observed in run fg1-oriole1). Only started when F1 saw the bus as ABL leaves it (gates on, USI I2C mode, pads function 2 and high, controller idle, FIFOs empty). The transfer registers it writes (ADDR, FIFO_CTL, INT_ENABLE, AUTO_CONF, CTL) are saved first and written back at the end, also after an error (after a soft reset when a transfer did not end). No gauge register is written. sweetfg=1 is unchanged.

